    "description": "1994 年索尼发布的首代家用主机，用 CD-ROM 取代卡带、把多边形 3D 图形变成家用机标配，是游戏机厅第五代主机与游戏大众化转折点的标志。",
    "category": "game-console",
    "sources": [
      {
        "type": "documentation",
        "title": "Wikipedia: PlayStation (console)",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PlayStation_(console)",
        "license": "cc",
        "accessed_at": "2026-11-20"
      },
      {
        "type": "documentation",
        "title": "Wikipedia: PlayStation",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PlayStation",
        "license": "cc",
        "accessed_at": "2026-11-20"
      },
      {
        "type": "documentation",
        "title": "Computer History Museum",
        "url": "https://www.computerhistory.org/",
        "license": "visual_reference_only",
        "accessed_at": "2026-11-20"
      }
    ],
    "intro": {
      "zh": "首代 PlayStation 是索尼 1994 年 12 月 3 日在日本发售的家用游戏机，用 650MB 的 CD-ROM 取代卡带、把多边形 3D 图形带进千家万户，让游戏从儿童娱乐走向 18 岁以上的成人主流市场。它是游戏机厅第五代主机的锚点，也是索尼成为行业霸主的第一战。",
      "en": "The original PlayStation, released by Sony in Japan on December 3, 1994, replaced cartridges with 650MB CD-ROMs and brought polygon 3D graphics into every living room, pushing gaming from a children's pastime into mainstream adult culture."
    },
    "era": 1994,
    "manufacturer": "Sony"
  },
  "assemblies": [
